<title>USA: N.Y. metal futures opening forecasts.</title>
<headline>N.Y. metal futures opening forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Precious metals and copper futures were called to open by floor traders as follows:</p>
<p>Gold - $1.00 to $2.00 an ounce lower</p>
<p>Silver - down 3.0 to 5.0 cents</p>
<p>Platinum - off $0.30 to $0.50</p>
<p>Palladium - $0.20 to $0.30 weaker</p>
<p>Copper - up 0.20 to 0.50 cent a lb</p>
<p>--New York Commodities Desk 212-859-1640</p>
</text>
